Added `src/router/smart-router/bench.test.ts` to verify that for a default `new Hono()` application (`src/hono.ts:26-33`, which configures `SmartRouter` with `[new RegExpRouter(), new TrieRouter()]`):

1. With only ordinary routes registered, `SmartRouter` selects `RegExpRouter` (`app.router.name === 'SmartRouter + RegExpRouter'`, `src/router/smart-router/router.ts:32-58`).
2. When a route that `RegExpRouter` cannot handle (such as `/files/:name{.*}`, which throws `UnsupportedPathError` at `src/router/reg-exp-router/node.ts:84-86` and `src/router/reg-exp-router/router.ts:62-65`) is registered, `SmartRouter` catches `UnsupportedPathError` (`src/router/smart-router/router.ts:39-44`), falls back to `TrieRouter` (`app.router.name === 'SmartRouter + TrieRouter'`), and answers requests accurately.
3. Adding a route after the first request has been handled throws `Error(MESSAGE_MATCHER_IS_ALREADY_BUILT)` (`'Can not add a route since the matcher is already built.'`, `src/router/smart-router/router.ts:13-16`).

